Phase 6A §2.1: real per-service memory at idle.

$ docker stats --no-stream --format "table {{.Name}}\t{{.MemUsage}}\t{{.MemPerc}}"
NAME                            MEM USAGE / LIMIT     MEM %
ledgerlight-phase0-postgres-1   2.339GiB / 7.355GiB   31.80%
ledgerlight-phase0-garage-1     94.77MiB / 7.355GiB   1.26%

Context: these two containers had been running continuously for 8+
hours at the time of this measurement, spanning the whole multi-phase
session (Phase 5 §8 through Phase 6A §1) -- postgres's 2.339GiB figure
is real accumulated shared_buffers/page-cache usage over that uptime,
not a fresh-start baseline. A fresh `docker compose up` would start
measurably lower; this is the real number this long-lived dev instance
actually shows right now, which is the figure that matters for
deciding whether this host has real headroom for the heavier e2e-lite
run.

api/worker/web were not running at measurement time (no built images
exist locally -- removed after Phase 5's own §5/§7 verification,
confirmed via `docker images`) -- no idle figures to report for them
yet; they will be measured on first real build+start under the
e2e-lite profile.

Real host memory at the time of this measurement (`Get-CimInstance
Win32_OperatingSystem`): 0.46GB free out of 15.2GB total -- critically
low, from the user's own other running applications (Firefox's many
processes alone measured ~4.3GB; vmmemWSL, this project's own Docker
VM, measured 1.14GB real total, consistent with the two containers
above, not the source of the pressure). Flagged directly to the user
via AskUserQuestion rather than attempting a build under this
constraint; the user chose to pause the heavy steps (build, Playwright,
ZAP) until memory headroom improves, and to proceed with the safe,
execution-free parts of §2 in the meantime (this measurement, and the
e2e-lite compose override file itself).

PENDING, once real memory headroom allows:
- api/worker/web idle memory, right after a fresh `docker compose
  ... up -d --build postgres garage api web` under the e2e-lite
  profile.
- Memory under real e2e load (the full Playwright suite running
